      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on this embedded c++ project for an automotive sensor module and i'm hitting a wall. the system has about 512MB of ram but it's slowly leaking. it takes like 4-5 hours of continuous operation before we hit an OOM error. i've checked the main loop and it looks clean, but i can't find where the allocation isn't being freed. can you give me a systematic way to track this down in a constrained environment?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
